{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And when he stands</b> — the sense of וכעמדו is that he died close to thirty years [after his rise]." "<b>And shall be divided</b> — I have already explained it." "<b>Nor to his posterity</b> — its meaning is, nor to his son. Similarly: ואחריהם בפיהם ירצו סלה." "<b>Nor according to his dominion</b> — none of the four who ruled in his stead was like him in dominion." "<b>And to others beside these</b> — the sense of ולאחרים מלבד אלה is that he joined also others to the four kings who ruled in four places, as I have explained. And now I shall state a general principle: from the beginning of ויחזק מלך הנגב until וזרועים ממנו יעמדו וחללו המקדש המעוז, which explicitly refers to the destruction of the Second Temple — these are wars that have already passed, and to recall their details and to search the ancient books in the book of Joseph ben Gurion, even if we knew all its words, would not help us now to know what has passed. Therefore I shall explain the words and the senses in general terms, and after the destruction of the Temple I shall explain in detail until ובעת קץ, for from there onward are the future things that remain, as I shall explain."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "The cited phrase does not correspond to any known biblical verse; retained as quoted."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:58.272778357Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}